Subject: [PATCH] amend! Forward senders transform_sender leaves as they are

Forward a sender default_domain doesn't transform instead of moving it

`default_domain::transform_sender` returns a sender it doesn't
transform by value, where [exec.domain.default] returns
`std::forward<Sndr>(sndr)`. `connect` passes every sender through
`transform_sender` twice, once for the domain it completes in and once
for the one it starts in, so each layer of `connect` moves the sender's
data twice: connecting `then(then(then(just(c), f), f), f)` moves `c`
nine times.

This diff returns such a sender by reference instead, so that connecting
the example moves `c` once. A step that leaves alone a new sender an
earlier step returned by value still returns it by value, since a
reference to it would outlive it. Whether a transformation changed the
sender is now judged ignoring references and cv-qualifiers, as
[exec.snd.transform] does, and so is whether a domain's transformation
matches `default_domain`'s. `get_completion_signatures` and
`get_item_types` strip the rvalue reference from the transformed type,
so a sender's static `get_completion_signatures` member sees the same
`Self` as before.

The new tests check that `transform_sender` returns a sender it doesn't
transform as a reference of the argument's value category without
throwing, that a sender a domain replaces is returned by value even when
the replacement is then left alone, and that `connect` doesn't move a
sender it doesn't transform.

